1
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:03,000
Between the wind and the lion is the woman. For
her, half the world may go to war.

2
00:11:54,000 --> 00:12:00,000
The Wind and the Lion is a action, adventure,
drama film directed by John Milius.

3
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:57,000
At the beginning of the 20th century an American woman is abducted in Morocco by Berbers, and
the attempts to free her range from diplomatic pressure to military intervention.

4
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:54,000
Mulai Ahmed er Raisuli, played by Sean Connery.

5
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Eden Pedecaris, played by Candice Bergen.

6
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Theodore Roosevelt, played by Brian Keith.

7
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:45,000
John Hay, played by John Huston.

8
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:42,000
Samuel Gummere, played by Geoffrey Lewis.

9
00:53:33,000 --> 00:53:39,000
Capt. Jerome, played by Steve Kanaly.

10
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
The Wind and the Lion is a 1975 American epic historical adventure film written and directed by
John Milius, and starring Sean Connery, Candice Bergen, Brian Keith, and John Huston.

11
01:05:27,000 --> 01:05:33,000
The film is loosely based on the real-life Perdicaris affair of 1904.

12
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
Connery plays Mulai Ahmed er Raisuli, a Moroccan Berber rebel and anti-imperialist leader, and Bergen plays
his American hostage Eden Pedecaris, a fictional character inspired by Ion Hanford Perdicaris.

13
01:17:21,000 --> 01:17:27,000
Milius' second feature film as a director, it was produced by Herb
Jaffe for Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, and distributed in the U.S.

14
01:23:18,000 --> 01:23:24,000
by United Artists and internationally by Columbia Pictures.

15
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
It received generally positive reviews from critics,
and was a moderate commercial success.

16
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
Jerry Goldsmith’s film score received Academy Award,
BAFTA Award and Grammy Award nominations.

17
01:41:09,000 --> 01:41:15,000
Milius was nominated for a Writers Guild of America Award for his screenplay.

18
01:47:06,000 --> 01:47:12,000
The film explores themes of morocco, political
negotiations, historical fiction, desert, colonialism.

19
01:53:03,000 --> 01:53:09,000
The tone is emotional.
